          %p
            In this article, we explore
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal categories
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrine"} doctrine
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
            cartesian categories.
          %p
            It is convenient to discuss the case of categories with arbitrary small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            (or arbitrary small
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjunctions
            to work with. Then, we may cut down to finite products and derive some possibly unexpected bonuses involving
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          %h2#free_productcompletions_of_sets Free product-completions of sets
          %p
            We start by constructing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
            category with small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
            by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Prod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prod(S)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Prod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \,\colon\, S \to Ob(Prod(S))
            with the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with small products and a function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \,\colon\, S \to Ob(C)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            a unique product-preserving functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Prod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi \,\colon\, Prod(S) \to C
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = Ob(\Pi) \circ i
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set/S
            is
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small-complete+category"} small-cocomplete
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
